<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply fell $0.5 bln in Feb 10 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply fell $0.5 bln in Feb 10 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply fell $500 million in the February 10 week to $3,859.7 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $10.5 billion to $4,997.9 billion. M-1 fell $5.6 billion to $1,081.6 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,858.5 billion versus $3,853.6 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
